EDICT 0010: snd_dma.c and snd_mix.c on their portable path on every build

Category: build-independent behaviour, no change in results on Linux (the sound build, build.sh SOUND=1).
The Win32 parts of the sound code drive DirectSound through winquake.h, which needs DirectDraw, DirectSound and
SciTech MGL headers, and keep their own buffer (pDSBuf). The reference's sound goes to its own DMA buffer
(edict_snd.c), so every build takes the portable path: the same mixing, the same buffer, on Windows and Linux.

